  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - Commencement of development (Full Permission) - The development to which this permission relates shall be commenced not later than the expiration of 3 years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - Approved Plans - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans: [Site Location Plan, \r\nLBM Footway Crossing Application No: 022338, \r\nE100 Revision A, \r\nE101 Revision A,\r\nEA Householder FRA.]",
    "Condition : 3 - Materials as Specified - The facing materials to be used for the development hereby permitted shall be those specified in the application form unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 4 - The development hereby approved shall implement the flood mitigation measures as submitted with the proposal titled: EA Householder FRA. These measures shall thereafter be retained in perpetuity.\r\n\r\nReason:  To reduce the risk of flooding and to comply with the following Local Plan 2024 policies for Merton: F15.7 and F15.8.",
    "Condition : 5 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant -Approved Schemes\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the National Planning Policy Framework, London Borough of Merton (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to the delivery of sustainable development, by:\r\n1. Providing a formal pre-application advice service, details to be found on Planning pre-application advice service on LBM's website\r\n2. Providing written policies and guidance, which is available to view on LBM's website.\r\n3. Where appropriate, negotiating amendments to secure a positive decision.\r\n4. Determining applications in a timely manner including providing a fast track service, details to be found on Get a quicker planning decision on LBM's website.\r\n\r\nIn this instance:\r\ni) The application was acceptable as submitted, and approved without delay.\r\n\r\n"
